{"task_id":"gsm8k-shuffled-1156","question":"Heather bought a jumbo bag of raisins with 27 cups of raisins in it. She wants to make oatmeal cookies, granola, and snack mix with the raisins. A batch of oatmeal cookies takes 3/4 of a cup of raisins. How many batches of oatmeal cookies can Heather make if she divides the bag of raisins equally among the cookies, granola, and snack mix?","your_frozen_proposal":{"rationale":"First, we need to determine how many cups of raisins Heather will use for each of the three recipes. Since she divides the bag of raisins equally among the recipes, we divide the total number of cups (27) by 3. Then, we calculate how many batches of oatmeal cookies can be made with the raisins intended for cookies. Each batch of oatmeal cookies takes 3/4 of a cup of raisins. So, we divide the raisins intended for cookies by the amount needed per batch.

